<title>UK: Cazenove Indian GDR Index little changed.</title>
<headline>Cazenove Indian GDR Index little changed.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cazenove Indian GDR Index rose 0.17 points, 0.24 percent, to 69.89 points with the Bombay Stock Exchange closed for a festival.</p>
<p>The premium for GDRs over stocks on the local market was 14.19 percent.</p>
<p>The Cazenove index is a capitalisation weighted basket of Indian global depositary receipts and measures the change from midday on the previous trading day to midday today.</p>
<p>-- David Chance, London newsroom +44 171 542 5887</p>
</text>
